# Direct runtime dependencies for the data-processing container image.
#
# This file is the source of truth for the image build. It contains ONLY
# runtime dependencies (dev/test tooling such as pytest, black, mypy, ruff,
# flake8, pre-commit and type stubs are intentionally excluded to keep the
# image slim - developers should use requirements.txt for local work).
#
# Regenerate the hash-pinned lockfile (all transitives included) targeting
# the container platform (Python 3.9, linux x86_64) with:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements-docker.in -o requirements.lock \
#       --generate-hashes \
#       --python-version 3.9 \
#       --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu \
#       --index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
#       --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu \
#       --index-strategy unsafe-best-match
#
# CI verifies the lockfile is up to date by re-running the command above and
# diffing against the committed file.

